# deploy/public/logrotate-aramo — host logrotate policy for the Aramo public-site
# containers (PR-D item 4; ratified 30-day log retention, counsel brief §2.1).
#
# WHY: the published Website Privacy Policy commits to keeping server logs for
# 30 days and then deleting them. Policy, config, and PRACTICE must agree — this
# file is the practice. nginx (public-web) sends its access/error logs to
# stdout/stderr, which Docker captures as json-file logs on the host; the intake
# handler does the same. This rotates those daily and keeps 30 days, deleting
# older. The compose `logging` caps (max-size × max-file) are a separate,
# size-based disk-fill backstop; THIS file is the time-based retention guarantee.
#
# INSTALL (bring-up runbook): copy to /etc/logrotate.d/aramo (root-owned, 0644).
# logrotate's daily cron then enforces it. `copytruncate` is required because
# Docker holds the log file descriptor open — logrotate copies then truncates in
# place rather than renaming out from under the daemon.

/var/lib/docker/containers/*/*-json.log {
  daily
  rotate 30
  missingok
  notifempty
  compress
  delaycompress
  copytruncate
  dateext
  su root root
}
